Subject: [PATCH] Generate valid unique GoogleTest parameter names

The sealed compiler test harness emits names such as mobilenet-v2_VPUX.3720.
System GoogleTest 1.17 rejects punctuation before any tests can run. Normalize
names to ASCII letters, digits and underscores, and append the parameter index
to avoid collisions after normalization. Parameters and test bodies are unchanged.

Applies to NPU compiler 6a7a7c531f54baed1dddfda1b80299413c4c6943.
Regression: actual-header registration fails on the original and checks names
that collide after normalization; the full compiler listing exercises bundled
configs without dropping cases.

--- a/src/vpux_driver_compiler/test/functional/vcl_tests_common.h
+++ b/src/vpux_driver_compiler/test/functional/vcl_tests_common.h
@@ -62,7 +62,17 @@
         auto netInfo = std::get<0>(param);
         const std::string netName = netInfo.at("network");
         const std::string deviceID = netInfo.at("device");
-        return netName + std::string("_VPUX.") + deviceID;
+        std::string name = netName + "_VPUX_" + deviceID;
+        for (auto& character : name) {
+            const bool alphanumeric = (character >= 'A' && character <= 'Z') ||
+                                      (character >= 'a' && character <= 'z') ||
+                                      (character >= '0' && character <= '9');
+            if (!alphanumeric && character != '_') {
+                character = '_';
+            }
+        }
+        // Distinct parameters can normalize to the same spelling.
+        return name + "_" + std::to_string(obj.index);
     }
 
